       the differences described on this page.

       The  pptthhrreeaadd__ttrryyjjooiinn__nnpp() function performs a nonblocking join with the
       thread _t_h_r_e_a_d, returning the exit status of the thread in _*_r_e_t_v_a_l.   If
       _t_h_r_e_a_d  has not yet terminated, then instead of blocking, as is done by
       pptthhrreeaadd__jjooiinn(3), the call returns an error.

       The pptthhrreeaadd__ttiimmeeddjjooiinn__nnpp() function performs a  join‐with‐timeout.   If
       _t_h_r_e_a_d  has  not  yet  terminated, then the call blocks until a maximum
       time, specified in _a_b_s_t_i_m_e, measured against the CCLLOOCCKK__RREEAALLTTIIMMEE  clock.
       If  the  timeout  expires before _t_h_r_e_a_d terminates, the call returns an
       error.  The _a_b_s_t_i_m_e argument is a ttiimmeessppeecc(3) structure, specifying  an
       absolute time measured since the Epoch (see ttiimmee(2)).

