       The pptthhrreeaadd__ttiimmeeddjjooiinn__nnpp() function measures time by internally
       calculating a relative sleep interval that is then measured against the
       CCLLOOCCKK__MMOONNOOTTOONNIICC clock instead of the CCLLOOCCKK__RREEAALLTTIIMMEE clock.
       Consequently, the timeout is unaffected by discontinuous changes to the
       CCLLOOCCKK__RREEAALLTTIIMMEE clock.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
       The following code waits to join for up to 5 seconds:

           struct timespec ts;
           int s;

           ...

           if (clock_gettime(CLOCK_REALTIME, &ts) == -1) {
               /* Handle error */
           }

           ts.tv_sec += 5;

           s = pthread_timedjoin_np(thread, NULL, &ts);
           if (s != 0) {
               /* Handle error */
           }

